n  technology is providing a possibility of  authenticating people so what we're  looking into is different avenues for  authenticating accounts so the idea is  that we make it very difficult to create  fake accounts to create unauthentic  accounts and then if a rating drops down  then that review that account isn't as  useful anymore in terms of spreading  propaganda or getting people to believe  something because the accounts already  seen as untrustworthy and it's difficult  to create a new fake one yeah I mean I  guess that has to be balanced with user  abandonment if it's too annoying to  create a new account yeah it does when  you heard Alon Musk's idea of a website  where some of the goals seem to be  similar although it seemed he must was  maybe more focused on the specific  content of articles as opposed to sort  of the general trustworthiness of a news  website in what ways is what you're  doing similar to what you on must  mentioned and in what ways is it not the  same thing I would say it's similar in  that we want to generate ratings for  articles the  authors that wrote the articles and the  news outlets that provided the ability  to publish the articles I think there is  still a general similarity in wanting to  get out whether or not there are biases  or they're trying to like get across a  point or maybe manipulate persuade  people into thinking certain ways but  with the similarities end after that  because we don't want like I said we're  not trying to pursue truth in its pure  form because you know fact-checking is  one of those things where it's hard to  do an automated way we're still like 5  to 10 years out from having that working  super well and if you're gonna do actual  fact-checking you have to have real  people doing it and that takes a lot of  time and in today's society like it  moves very quickly and then the other  thing is that I don't know you know he  threw it out as an idea I don't know  exactly what his actual greater idea was  